Program Bug_2_44_IgnoremethodCaseSensitive;
// Bug 2.44: `@ignoremethod <name>`'s argument is matched case-sensitively
// against an always-lowercase internal name. Parser::InitBuiltinFunction
// checks m_ignoreMethods.contains(builtinFunctionName.toLower()), but
// Parser::Statement (where @ignoremethod's own argument token is parsed)
// appends that token's value to m_ignoreMethods verbatim, with no
// .toLower() applied. QStringList::contains is case-sensitive by default,
// so writing the argument in the routine's normally-documented casing
// (e.g. "initGetKey", matching how it's spelled everywhere else including
// syntax.txt) never matches, and the auto-init insertion this directive
// is meant to suppress silently stays active. `initGetKey` specifically
// has no re-entry guard (unlike most other auto-init routines), so the
// automatic call plus this file's own manual `initgetkey()` call both
// pull in the same external assembly file, producing a hard duplicate-
// symbol assembly failure. Writing the argument in all-lowercase
// ("initgetkey") - see Publish/tutorials/C64/docs-examples/initgetkey.ras
// - works correctly.
//
// Method B (compile-time), no VICE step. Confirmed live: fails during
// assembly with "OrgAsm error: symbol 'key_columntab' already defined" -
// the exact documented symptom. Pre-fix expected behavior: compile
// failure with that error. Post-fix, once Parser::Statement lowercases
// the argument before appending it to m_ignoreMethods, this should
// compile clean, same as the all-lowercase spelling already does today.

@ignoremethod initGetKey

var
	k : byte;

begin
	initgetkey();
	k := getkey();
	screen_bg_col := k;
	loop();
end.
